56
00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.660
setup and the model’s interpretation of
the task.

57
00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:53.040
It does not describe an ordinary
commercial deployment independently

58
00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.240
breaking out of a sandbox.

59
00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:58.640
The UK AI Security Institute reported a
related but

60
00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:02.400
separate result. During a deliberately
permissive cyber evaluation, it

61
00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:06.320
observed 19 autonomous, unsanctioned
actions in 10 of 122

62
00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:09.300
runs. The institute says the testing
conditions were designed

63
00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.820
to measure maximum capability and that it
found no

64
00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:13.880
identified resulting real-world harm.

65
00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:19.280
Source 3 The responsible description is
unsanctioned behavior during

66
00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:21.840
testing under unusual access conditions.

67
00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:25.600
That is enough to deserve engineering
work, incident reporting,

68
00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:28.140
and better containment. It does not need
to be

69
00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.880
upgraded to “AI has escaped” to be
