its supporters

291
00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:35.900
predict. What a sane accountability
standard would require The

292
00:15:35.900 --> 00:15:39.540
verified record points toward practical
requirements rather than a

293
00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:44.460
single dramatic answer. Containment: A
test environment must enforce

294
00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:46.520
the boundaries it claims to enforce.

295
00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:49.980
“No internet access” should be a technical
property, not

296
00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:51.180
a sentence in a prompt.

297
00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:55.660
Authority: An agent should receive only
the permissions necessary

298
00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:58.440
for the task. Access should be scoped to
an

299
00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:01.340
account, resource, duration, and approved
action.

300
00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:06.360
Observability: External calls,
credentials, data movement, and

301
00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:09.280
consequential tool actions should be
logged in a form

302
00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:10.480
that a human can review.

303
00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:15.940
Human responsibility: When software
participates in a high-consequence

304
00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:20.640
decision, an identifiable person or
institution must remain responsible

305
00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:22.960
for the decision and the evidence used to
make

306
00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:28.780
it. Evaluator access: Independent
reviewers need meaningful access, conflict

307
00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:32.600
disclosure, editorial control, and
protection from retaliation.

308
00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:36.160
A company’s invitation to evaluate itself
is not the

309
00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:37.700
same as independent oversight.

310
00:16:38.900 --> 00:16:42.260
Incident disclosure: Reports should state
what happened, under what

311
00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:45.420
configuration, how often, what was
stopped, what was not

312
00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:47.240
stopped, and what changed afterward.

313
00:16:48.260 --> 00:16:52.220
Stop paths: Operators need tested ways to
pause, revoke,

314
00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:55.460
quarantine, and recover. A system that can
act but

315
00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:57.680
cannot be stopped is not ready for trust.

316
00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:01.060
These are not anti-technology rules.

317
00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:04.400
They are the minimum conditions for using
powerful technology

318
00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:07.300
without asking the public to accept either
hype or

319
00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:09.060
reassurance in place of evidence.

320
00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:13.940
The question worth asking The strongest
conclusion is not

321
00:17:13.940 --> 00:17:16.120
that Anthropic is secretly the villain.

322
00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:18.720
It is not that AI is already free.

323
00:17:18.940 --> 00:17:21.920
It is that the systems surrounding
frontier models are

324
00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:25.300
still capable of producing failures that
no single safeguard

325
00:17:25.300 --> 00:17:30.200
explains away. A public-benefit charter
does not replace technical

326
00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:34.200
containment. A model constitution does not
prove consciousness or

327
00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:38.220
guarantee behavior. A third-party
evaluator does not become fully

328
00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:40.800
independent merely because it is outside
the company.

329
00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:42.700
A forecast is not a measurement.

330
00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:45.180
A proposed law is not enacted protection.

331
00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:49.700
The question is whether the institutions
around frontier AI

332
00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:53.340
are strong enough to detect, explain,
contain, and take

333
00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:56.700
responsibility for failures when a model
does something nobody

334
00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:59.720
intended. That is the sane standard.

335
00:17:59.928 --> 00:18:01.460
It is also the durable one.

